# Accepted hygiene findings.
#
# A finding with an exceptional modeling justification can be accepted here after review.
# Each suppression names the affected resource (iof-h:focusNode) and the rule that fired
# (iof-h:rule): a constraint such as iof-h:RoleDefinedByBearerEquivalentTo, or a whole
# shape such as iof-h:RoleDefinedByBearer to cover all its axiom forms. The rdfs:comment
# justification is required. hygiene_runner.py still prints a suppressed finding, as a
# notice with the justification, so it stays visible but no longer fails or warns.
#
# Example:
#
#   [] a iof-h:Suppression ;
#       iof-h:focusNode iof-constr:SomeRole ;
#       iof-h:rule iof-h:RoleDefinedByBearerEquivalentTo ;
#       rdfs:comment "Why this definition is intended, and who reviewed it." .

@prefix iof-constr: <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/> .
@prefix iof-h: <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/hygiene/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xs: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

